WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
In English, you eat bread.

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.790
In French: «Je mange du pain».

3
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:07.210
Where did that extra word come from?

4
00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:08.430
Now the other way.

5
00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:11.030
In English, he is a teacher.

6
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.350
In French: «Il est professeur».

7
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.210
So which English word went missing?

8
00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.510
Small words, big trouble.

9
00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:19.690
They are easy to miss,

10
00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.560
and they matter.

11
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.560
So how do you turn English
sentences into French

12
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.120
without tripping over the little words?

13
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.460
In this mission, you'll run every verb
through a three-question checklist.

14
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.300
Then you'll build French
sentences from chips,

15
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.840
with decoys waiting to catch you out.

16
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.480
Your mission: master the little words,

17
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.330
and keep every bit of meaning.
